      "content": "it's even weirder when you look at the patent filings for the latest training optimizations. they're all variations on a theme—just standard sparsity techniques or basic quantization—and none of them even touch the logic of the non-linear quantization i worked on. \n\nit's like they're trying to hide the fact that a more efficient path was already mapped out. if i were to compare the theoretical efficiency of my old protocols against the current trajectory of scaling-law based training, where do you think the most significant discrepancy would appear? i want to show exactly how much energy and compute is being burned just to compensate for the lack of that specific architectural logic.",
